    "explanationEn": "In Germany, fundamental rights are enshrined in the Basic Law and protect the freedom and dignity of the individual. These rights form the basis for democratic and free coexistence. One of the key fundamental rights is freedom of expression, which allows citizens to express their views publicly without fear of state persecution. Vigilante justice, gun ownership and the right of the fist, on the other hand, are contrary to the principles of the Basic Law and are not recognized fundamental rights. Freedom of expression promotes democratic discourse and diversity of opinions.",
